WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.904
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:06.292 --> 00:00:08.460
SPEAKER: Once we have
our APIs enabled,

00:00:08.460 --> 00:00:12.540
head to the IoT Core page
to create a device registry.

00:00:12.540 --> 00:00:14.910
Give it a name, and choose
your closest region,

00:00:14.910 --> 00:00:16.395
then use MQTT protocol.

00:00:18.980 --> 00:00:22.690
Under Default Telemetry
Topic, create a new topic.

00:00:22.690 --> 00:00:24.850
Give that a name, then
click Create to create

00:00:24.850 --> 00:00:27.430
your new device registry
with an associated Pub/Sub

00:00:27.430 --> 00:00:31.010
topic for publishing
the telemetry events.

00:00:31.010 --> 00:00:35.310
Now switch to your terminal
to generate a device key pair.

00:00:35.310 --> 00:00:37.460
Back to the IoT Core
registry details page.

00:00:37.460 --> 00:00:39.640
We will add a device.

00:00:39.640 --> 00:00:43.280
Go to the Devices tab,
then click Create a Device.

00:00:43.280 --> 00:00:46.960
Enter a device ID, and
then choose RS256_X509 5

00:00:46.960 --> 00:00:50.790
under the Public Key Format.

00:00:50.790 --> 00:00:53.340
Get the text from the
rsa_cert.pem file that you

00:00:53.340 --> 00:00:56.490
generated earlier, including
the BEGIN CERTIFICATE and END

00:00:56.490 --> 00:00:59.640
CERTIFICATE lines, and paste
it into the Public Key Value

00:00:59.640 --> 00:01:00.775
field.

00:01:00.775 --> 00:01:02.775
Click Create to add this
device to the registry.

00:01:05.459 --> 00:01:07.730
Now, you'll run some code
and connect to this device

00:01:07.730 --> 00:01:10.720
and view the telemetry data.

00:01:10.720 --> 00:01:14.890
Grab this node code from
GitHub for IoT Core.

00:01:14.890 --> 00:01:18.610
Navigate to the
mqtt_example folder.

00:01:18.610 --> 00:01:22.460
Copy the private key from
before to this folder.

00:01:22.460 --> 00:01:26.460
Then install the
node dependencies.

00:01:26.460 --> 00:01:28.520
Now you can create a
subscription to the Pub/Sub

00:01:28.520 --> 00:01:31.740
topic that this registry uses.

00:01:31.740 --> 00:01:34.800
Next, connect to the virtual
device with the Cloud IoT Core

00:01:34.800 --> 00:01:38.323
over the MQTT bridge.

00:01:38.323 --> 00:01:39.740
If everything is
set up correctly,

00:01:39.740 --> 00:01:43.490
you'll now see 25 payload
messages published.

00:01:43.490 --> 00:01:45.350
Check the Pub/Sub
topic now to confirm

00:01:45.350 --> 00:01:47.950
it's getting messages
published to it.

00:01:47.950 --> 00:01:50.230
You can run that Pub/Sub
subscriptions pull command

00:01:50.230 --> 00:01:52.720
again to get more messages.

00:01:52.720 --> 00:01:53.830
And congratulations.

00:01:53.830 --> 00:01:55.913
You've got your Internet
of Things service running

00:01:55.913 --> 00:01:57.540
on Google Cloud.

